## Tasks

<% if tasks.github %>
- `TASKS.md` is a read-only view of GitHub issues: never edit it; `just task sync` refreshes it.
- Start of session: follow the rules at the top of `TASKS.md`, read *Active* and continue from the latest journal line; every task names a model tier and reasoning effort.
- Work through `just task` (list, next, start #n, log #n "text" --resume "next step", done #n, new "title"). Done = implemented + `just check` green + reviewed; the PR closes the issue.
<% else %>
- Start of session: follow the rules at the top of `TASKS.md`, read *Active* and continue from the resume point unless told otherwise; every task names a model tier and reasoning effort.
- Work through `just task` (list, next, start T-012, log T-012 "text" --resume "next step", done T-012, new "title"); on stop run `just task log <id> "what changed" --resume "next step" --progress 60`.
<% if tasks.both %>
- Done = implemented + `just check` green + reviewed; then `just task done <id>`. `just task sync` mirrors tasks to GitHub issues (one way); never edit the mirrored issues by hand.
<% else %>
- Done = implemented + `just check` green + reviewed; then `just task done <id>`.
<% end %>
<% end %>
